{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-35318" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,$ then $\\text{nullity}(A)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-35318" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that by definition, $\\text{nullity}(A)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A)).$\n\nTo find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))$, we reduce $A$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 13 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(A)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-35318" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ceddfda5213b9f41c8c3cffba6c5c6f22475e4594ef51317c51c9fecad8b3ed2"} {"question" "q-35318" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-35318" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-35318" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-35348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given $Z=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,$ what is $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Z))?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-35348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Z))$, we reduce $Z$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Z & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{5} & :={R}_{5}+(-\\frac{2}{3}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $4$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $4$th column). \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Z))=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-35348" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ceddfda5213b9f41c8c3cffba6c5c6f22475e4594ef51317c51c9fecad8b3ed2"} {"question" "q-35348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-35348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-35348" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-35349" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrices given below. Find $\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C)).$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-35349" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has $2$ pivot columns and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $4$th columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=2.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has $4$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1+2+0=3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-35349" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ceddfda5213b9f41c8c3cffba6c5c6f22475e4594ef51317c51c9fecad8b3ed2"} {"question" "q-35349" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-35349" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-35349" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-79336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $Q$ be a $5\\times 8$ matrix that has $5$ pivot columns. What is the dimension of the null space of $Q?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-79336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(Q))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $Q.$ \n\nSince $Q$ has $8$ columns and $5$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $Q$ is \n\n$$\n8-5=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(Q))=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-79336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ceddfda5213b9f41c8c3cffba6c5c6f22475e4594ef51317c51c9fecad8b3ed2"} {"question" "q-79336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-79336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-79336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-139974" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrices given below. Find $\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C)).$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 8 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-139974" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $3$rd columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd  column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C))=2+1+1=4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af042710ce7cc1ead419395f147a4a526fc9"} {"question" "q-139974" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ceddfda5213b9f41c8c3cffba6c5c6f22475e4594ef51317c51c9fecad8b3ed2"} {"question" "q-139974" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075477/state.json" "file_sha256" "4e3fe3c9ebcb06068d52d28ceb21af0